            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0770" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3094: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-04T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>356. Messrs. Sullivan and Cromwell complain that contrary to terms of Pacific
                    Development loan contract of November 28 [<hi rendition="#italic">26</hi>],
                        1919,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d670-f1"/> the Chinese Government has failed to
                    deposit the necessary interest with the Chase National Bank which was due
                    December 1st. It is desired that you bring this matter to the attention of the
                    Chinese Government pointing out the very serious effect which such a default has
                    upon the financial credit of China and upon any measures of financial assistance
                    which may be in contemplation. You should urge the immediate remedying of the
                    default.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
